  <article class="prose">
    <section>
      <h2>The Problem: The Collapse of Code Authenticity</h2>
      <p>
        Generative AI tooling has made it trivial for candidates to paste AI-generated solutions into coding interviews and hackathons without understanding core algorithms. Traditional string-distance checkers (such as Levenshtein or token-based Moss) fail to catch LLM completions because variable renaming, whitespace shifts, and comment additions scramble token sequences.
      </p>
      <p>
        At the same time, traditional certification platforms issue easily forged PDF credentials. Chaincode was built at HackIndia to solve both sides of this trust equation: detecting semantic code provenance and anchoring verified achievement to an immutable decentralized ledger.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Dual-Tier Architecture: AI Evaluation + Smart Contracts</h2>
      <p>
        The platform operates as a secure two-tier pipeline separating off-chain algorithmic computation from on-chain certificate consensus:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tier 1 (Off-Chain Analysis):</strong> Submissions are ingested via Next.js serverless functions, tokenized, and evaluated against Gemini AI with a constrained system prompt to isolate algorithmic logic from cosmetic variable alterations. The engine checks time complexity, auxiliary space allocation, and semantic originality.</li>
        <li><strong>Tier 2 (On-Chain Minting):</strong> If the evaluation passes both runtime correctness tests and the 90%+ originality threshold, the backend signs an authorization voucher. The developer’s Web3 wallet (MetaMask) calls the Solidity smart contract on EVM to mint an ERC-721 token storing IPFS metadata, timestamp, and challenge ID.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Smart Contract Engineering (Solidity)</h2>
      <p>
        The ERC-721 contract implements gas-optimized cryptographic signature verification (EIP-712). Rather than writing expensive string payloads directly to the blockchain, the contract stores a cryptographic hash of the challenge result pointing to decentralized IPFS storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        Key smart contract guarantees:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Replay Protection:</strong> Each signature voucher contains a unique nonce and sender address, preventing unauthorized wallet re-use.</li>
        <li><strong>Gas Optimization:</strong> Custom bitmasking for status flags reduces mint gas costs below 65,000 gas units per certificate.</li>
        <li><strong>Decentralized Metadata:</strong> Token URIs resolve to permanent IPFS hashes with standard OpenSea metadata attributes (Rank, Problem ID, Efficiency Score).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Chaincode vs Traditional Code Checkers</h2>
      <table class="comparison-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Dimension</th>
